Ubuntu Drime Backup is an independent project maintained by deathferre-cloud.
It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Drime or rclone.

The project uses rclone v1.75.1, licensed under the MIT license.
Its license and attribution are reproduced in licenses/rclone-MIT.txt.
The rclone-patches directory modifies the upstream Drime backend and adds tests.
scripts/build-rclone.sh fetches the pinned upstream source and applies those
changes. The generated client is identified as v1.75.1-ubuntu-drime.2.

Go and rclone dependencies retain their respective upstream licenses.
This source release does not bundle the Go toolchain or upstream dependency
source trees. The build fetches them using the pinned source and module data.
